      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/WorldPowerDesk/status/2041981153268441193",
      "text": "🚨 Update: The situation in the Strait of Hormuz has reached a new level:\n\nThe past 12 hours have changed everything.\n\n– Iran reopened the Strait of Hormuz this morning under the ceasefire agreement, and two oil tankers passed through safely.\n\n– Israel launched more than 100 airstrikes on Lebanon hours later, in the largest attack since the start of the war. One of the strikes killed 112 people.\n\n– Iran has re-closed the Strait of Hormuz, and oil tanker traffic has completely stopped.\n\n– Al Jazeera confirmed that Iran is \"considering a complete withdrawal from the ceasefire.\"\n\n– Iranian armed forces have begun identifying targets inside Israel, according to Shafaq News.\n\n– Oil prices fell by 19% this morning following the ceasefire announcement, the biggest drop since 2020, and uncertainty has returned.\n\n– Pete Hegseth said: \"Iran begged for a ceasefire,\" and now Iran is preparing to withdraw from it.\n\nMore than 150 ships were stranded at the height of the previous shutdown, and shipping traffic plummeted from 150 vessels per day to fewer than 20.\n\nGasoline prices in California reached $6 per gallon. The Philippines is operating on a four-day work week. Japan is releasing its emergency reserves.\n\nThe ceasefire lasted 12 hours. The Strait of Malacca, through which 20% of the world's oil passes, was closed again. There are no signs of it reopening.\n\nI'll keep you updated. Turn on notifications.",
